"""
DISSERTATION TITLE: 
An Ensemble Machine Learning Approach to Quantitative Trading: 
Integrating GARCH Volatility with XGBoost and LightGBM

RESEARCH QUESTIONS:
1. Can GARCH volatility features improve ensemble machine learning predictions?
2. Does the XGBoost-LightGBM ensemble outperform individual models?
3. How do different volatility regimes affect model performance?
4. Is the hybrid approach robust across market cycles?

THEORETICAL FRAMEWORK:
- Volatility Modeling: GARCH (Bollerslev, 1986)
- Ensemble Learning: XGBoost (Chen & Guestrin, 2016)
- Gradient Boosting: LightGBM (Ke et al., 2017)
- Market Efficiency: Adaptive Market Hypothesis (Lo, 2004)
- Behavioral Finance: Prospect Theory (Kahneman & Tversky, 1979)

KEY LITERATURE:
- Bollerslev, T. (1986). Generalized autoregressive conditional heteroskedasticity.
- Chen, T., & Guestrin, C. (2016). XGBoost: A scalable tree boosting system.
- Ke, G., et al. (2017). LightGBM: A highly efficient gradient boosting decision tree.
- López de Prado, M. (2018). Advances in Financial Machine Learning.
"""

